{#
  BeMart Password-reset page — EC-CUBE goResetPassword.

  PORT of EC-CUBE 4.3 default-theme `Forgot/reset.twig`
  (src/Eccube/Resource/template/default/Forgot/reset.twig).

  Markup skeleton, `ec-registerRole` / `ec-pageHeader` / `ec-off1Grid` /
  `ec-borderedDefs` / `ec-input` / `ec-registerRole__actions` /
  `ec-off4Grid` classes + the <dl>/<dt>/<dd> definition-list structure
  are kept verbatim from EC-CUBE.

  Phase 3 — FORM page (Ray.WebFormModule). The Reset resource exposes a
  real `ResetForm` (an AbstractForm) as `body.form`; the inputs are
  rendered through it:

    {{ form.input('password')|raw }}   <- real <input> w/ name/attrs
    {{ form.error('password') }}       <- inline Be-domain error

  EC-CUBE renders the same inputs through the Symfony FormView
  (`form_widget(form.password.first)`); the render-diff test stubs
  EC-CUBE's `form_widget` to delegate to the SAME ResetForm, so the
  inputs diff to ZERO. Validation authority stays with the Be Framework
  Becoming chain (ResetPasswordInput Semantics + ResetKeyInvalid).

  MISSING-FIELD NOTE — EC-CUBE's `PasswordResetType` has a `login_email`
  field (the confirmation email the user re-enters). BeMart's
  `ResetPasswordInput` models `resetKey` + `password`, NOT email — the
  reset is keyed by `resetKey`. The `login_email` <dl> row is rendered
  for fidelity (ResetForm declares the field as a renderer field) but has
  no BeMart body field; flagged as a missing-body-field residual.

  EC-CUBE-ism rebinding (see var/templates/README.md):
   - `{{ 'key'|trans }}`  -> the ja literal from messages.ja.yaml.
   - `form._token` — Symfony CSRF widget; kept as a hidden input with an
     empty value (BeMart's html context has no CSRF widget).
   - `resetKey` — carried from the emailed reset link's query param into
     a hidden field for the POST. The Login.html.twig pilot keeps the
     same hidden-input convention.
   - `error` — EC-CUBE's reset template shows a top-level `error` block;
     BeMart renders the form-level `message` (set by Reset::onPost on a
     domain rejection) in the same `ec-errorMessage` <p>.
   - `has_errors(...)` — request-validation runtime; false on a fresh
     form, so the conditional ` error` class never appears.
#}
{# EC-CUBE's Forgot/reset.twig does NOT set body_class, so the
   default_frame.twig default `other_page` applies. #}
{% extends 'base.html.twig' %}

{% set route = 'forgot_reset' %}
{% set title = 'パスワード再発行(再設定)' %}

{% block main %}
    <div class="ec-registerRole">
        <div class="ec-pageHeader">
            <h1>パスワード再発行(再設定)</h1>
        </div>
        <div class="ec-off1Grid">
            <div class="ec-off1Grid__cell">
                <form id="form1" method="post" novalidate>
                    <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrfToken|default('') }}">
                    <input type="hidden" name="resetKey" value="{{ resetKey|default('') }}">
                    <div class="ec-borderedDefs">
                        <dl>
                            <dt>
                                <label class="ec-label">メールアドレス</label>
                            </dt>
                            <dd>
                                <div class="ec-input">
                                    {{ form.input('login_email')|raw }}
                                    {{ form.error('login_email') }}
                                    {% if message is defined and message %}
                                        <p class="ec-errorMessage">{{ message }}</p>
                                    {% endif %}
                                </div>
                            </dd>
                        </dl>
                        <dl>
                            <dt>
                                <label class="ec-label">パスワード</label>
                            </dt>
                            <dd>
                                <div class="ec-input">
                                    {{ form.input('password')|raw }}
                                    {{ form.error('password') }}
                                </div>
                                <div class="ec-input">
                                    {{ form.input('password_confirm')|raw }}
                                    {{ form.error('password_confirm') }}
                                </div>
                            </dd>
                        </dl>
                    </div>
                    <div class="ec-registerRole__actions">
                        <div class="ec-off4Grid">
                            <div class="ec-off4Grid__cell">
                                <button class="ec-blockBtn--action" type="submit">登録する</button>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </form>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
{% endblock %}
